# Never ship mocks. Vite loads this for every production build — `pnpm build`,
# `make desktop`, CI, or a teammate checking something by hand — so the guard is
# a property of the UI project rather than of one caller's environment.
#
# It exists because it was needed. `main.tsx` starts MSW unless VITE_USE_MOCKS is
# exactly "false", so the first packaged build registered mockServiceWorker.js and
# rendered fixtures forever, never reading ~/.roster. It looked like a working
# board; the only symptom was that no /api request ever reached uvicorn. A fix
# passed on the `make desktop` command line was then bypassed within minutes by an
# ordinary `pnpm build` in projects/ui, which put the MSW chunk straight back.
#
# `pnpm dev` is unaffected: development mode does not read this file, so the
# mock-first default that lets the UI run with no backend still holds.
VITE_USE_MOCKS=false
